You can install LLDB (the LLVM debugger) on Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) with a single apt command.

1. One-Command Installation

bash
sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y lldb
Use code with caution.

2. Verify lldb Is Installed & Ready

bash
which lldb && lldb --version
Use code with caution.
(Note: If you plan to use lldb to attach to running processes on Ubuntu without sudo, remember that Ubuntu's kernel.yama.ptrace_scope defaults to 1; you can temporarily allow user-level attaching with echo 0 | sudo tee /proc/sys/kernel/yama/ptrace_scope.)
